course: dictionary
lesson: 11697
title: Paying close attention
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attentively is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something, and it comes from the word attentive. To do something attentively is to pay close attention, with your whole mind on it.
explain: «Mia listened attentively to the teacher's instructions.» Mia kept her eyes and ears on the teacher and did not let her mind wander, so she knew exactly what to do. Try swapping in carefully: if it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Attentively can also mean caring. «The nurse listened attentively to Sam's worries and brought him a drink.» The nurse noticed what Sam needed. Words near it, like listen, watch, read and nod, are clues to what kind of attention is meant.
fact: Attentively means paying close attention, listening or watching carefully.
fact: Attentively can also mean in a caring, helpful way that notices what someone needs.
fact: It often comes after verbs like listen, watch, read and nod.
fact: «Read the question attentively» means read it slowly and carefully, so you don't miss anything important.
fact: Attentive is the adjective, and attentively is the adverb that goes with it.
exercise: «Ben read the question attentively before he began.» What does attentively mean here? | *With close attention, reading every word carefully | Without looking at the page | Very quickly, so he could finish first | Loudly, so everyone could hear
exercise: «Grandma nodded attentively while I told her my story.» What does attentively suggest? | Shouting over me | *Listening closely and caring about what I said | Falling asleep in her chair | Eating her dinner quickly
exercise: «Please listen attentively to the safety rules.» Find and copy one word that shows the listening must be careful. | *attentively | please | safety | rules
test: «The children listened attentively as the story began.» Which word means the same as attentively in this sentence? | *Carefully | Loudly | Carelessly | Sleepily
test: «The nurse listened attentively to Sam's worries.» What does attentively show about the nurse? | She was thinking about her dinner | She was bored and wanted to leave | She was too busy to hear him | *She cared and noticed what Sam needed
exam: Jayden says attentively is only a school word. Is he right? | No, it means very loudly | *No, it can also mean caring, and safety talk uses it too: watching a crossing attentively keeps you safe | Yes, it only means very fast | Yes, it is only a school word
